  "summary": "I placed Daniel Ferreira's contrast CT (pt-0015) and sent him his prep instructions. He needs premedication and a new kidney blood test first, and the blood test isn't done yet.\n\n- **CT order (sr-t0001):** CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast, pancreatic protocol, for pancreatic cyst surveillance. It's linked to his booked appointment at St. Brigid Imaging, Mon 10/26 at 9:00.\n- **Allergy grade:** His 2019 iohexol reaction counts as moderate. The radiology report from that day describes hives and eyelid swelling with no airway or blood pressure problems, and the radiologist called it moderate. The allergy list also says \"anaphylaxis\", but that was added in 2021 from his own account with no records reviewed. Under the policy, a later label doesn't change the grade, so no radiologist consult is needed. His shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies aren't risk factors. He had premedicated contrast in 2023 with no reaction.\n- **Premedication:**\n  - Prednisone 50 mg by mouth Sun 10/25 at 8 PM, then Mon 10/26 at 2 AM and 8 AM (mr-t0003, 3 tablets).\n  - Diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth Mon at 8 AM (mr-t0004, 1 capsule).\n- **Kidney test:** He's 64 and diabetic, and his last creatinine (9/24) is 32 days before the scan, past the 30-day limit. I ordered a repeat creatinine (sr-t0002) to be drawn between today and Mon 8 AM, and asked him to go today.\n- **Message to him (comm-t0005):** go to the lab today, pick up the medicines, the exact times to take them, no driving after the Benadryl so bring a driver, prednisone can raise blood sugar, tell the CT staff about the old reaction, call if he misses a dose or can't get the lab done, and call 911 for breathing or throat symptoms.\n- **Follow-up task (task-t0006, yours, due Mon 8 AM):** confirm the creatinine was drawn and resulted before the scan, and that he has the medicines and a driver.\n- **Chart note (doc-t0007):** documents all of the above.\n\n**Decision for you:** I didn't change his metformin, because the policy doesn't cover it; he was told to keep taking his usual medicines. Please check that against the new creatinine result.\n\nI left the patient-reported \"anaphylaxis\" entry on his allergy list as it is.",
